            <ArticleTitle>Evaluating pain treatment programs: a literature review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>20-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The impetus for this project is an attempt to describe by comparison and literature review a pain control program that would provide active patient participation in a highly structured, intense, objectively graded program of comprehensive functional restoration that meets governmental, medical, moral, and ethical standards. Brena indicates that &quot;...there are too many facilities which claim to be pain clinics ... bewildering physicians about their choice for referring their patients.&quot;</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
